- In task .23, `skills/super-code/coordinator.js:25–27` leaves an omitted identity unresolved, and lines 740–747 require the existing Resume dispatch to return a safe identity before constructing Launch. Missing identity visibly throws. This implements the amended Task 20 contract; weakening that live-startup check would violate it.
- `dispatch-text.mjs` loads the coordinator’s actual builders with an AsyncFunction, inserts its return immediately before the round loop, and executes everything before that return. In .23, `loadBuilders` at lines 101–114 supplies an agent that always returns null. Thus Resume cannot mint or return an identity during builder loading.
- The caller at .23 lines 127–136 passes the persisted Launch identity only when `reviewOutput` is true. Non-review kinds omit it even when their ledger has a valid ID. Their loader therefore reaches the new missing-identity throw before returning builders. This affects implement, task review, verification-close, fix, seam-review, check-fix-review, merge, plan, triage, check-evidence, and non-final-review assembly. Task review is a non-review-output kind here: it uses task artifacts rather than the invocation final-review bundle.
